Third-party data
----------------
This repository does not contain third-party indicator lists or detection rules. They are downloaded by the
user's own computer, straight from their public sources, when an update is run, and they remain subject to the
terms of their authors:

- Mobile Verification Toolkit indicator index - https://github.com/mvt-project/mvt-indicators
  and the indicator files it lists, published by Amnesty International Security Lab, Citizen Lab and other
  research organisations (for example https://github.com/AmnestyTech/investigations).
- Stalkerware indicators by Echap - https://github.com/AssoEchap/stalkerware-indicators
- Zero Breach indicators - https://github.com/interplains/zero-breach
- signature-base YARA rules by Florian Roth / Nextron Systems (only with "scs update --yara"),
  Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/Neo23x0/signature-base

No source code of these projects is included. The detection approach follows the public documentation of
MVT and androidqf (Amnesty International Security Lab), TinyCheck and Zero Breach.
